    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d159">

                <pb facs="0374" n="304" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg304"/>

                <head>No. 159.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Denaut.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-09-22"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 22,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    note of the 12th instant, informing the Department that your Government had
                    determined to reconvene the conference upon the subject of protection to
                    submarine cables, for the purpose of concluding the project of a convention
                    drawn up in November last, and, in recognition of your accompanying request, to
                    signify the concurrence of this Government in the contemplated reunion upon
                    October 15 next.</p>
                <p>The delegates of the United States have accordingly been instructed to-day by
                    telegraph to attend the conference and conclude the proposed convention, and
                    that pending the receipt of formal full powers, which will be duly forwarded,
                    they will act upon the authority of their cable instructions.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
